  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1235 AM CDT Tue Aug 25 2026\n\nIncreasing Precipitation Chances Tuesday:\n\nLow level return flow through the Upper Missouri River Valley \nMonday night is advecting increased moisture upstream of the \nlocal forecast area through Minnesota with PWATs (RAOB/GOES-\nderived) above 1.5\" through the Dakotas into western Minnesota. \nUpper level water vapor imagery loops show a stout upper level \ntrough topping broad ridging across the western CONUS phasing \neast overnight into Tuesday morning, ushering in local \nprecipitation and storm chances through much of Tuesday.\n\nStorm Potential Tuesday:\n\nLocal severe storm threat remains low (<10%) due to main \ninstability axis of 1000+ J/kg MLCAPE traversing the local \nforecast area from the evening into the nighttime hours. While \naccompanying shear values remain high in the lowest levels \n(0-1km: 25kts, 0-3km: 20- 35kts), lack of coincidental timing \nwith peak diurnal heating lacks overall confidence for accessing\nthe strongest, near surface values. Therefore, a marginal risk \nfor the Storm Prediction Center persists for much of the \nforecast area.\n\nWeekend Precipitation Chances:\n\nThe synoptic trough advects low level cold air advection \nthrough the Upper Mississippi River Valley Wednesday, keeping \napparent temperatures mostly in the 70s to low 80s for much of \nthe local forecast area. Subsequent precipitation chances \nincrease through the weekend.",
